      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "LDL is often referred to as \"bad cholesterol\" because high levels can lead to plaque buildup in your arteries, which can increase the risk of heart disease. HDL, or \"good cholesterol,\" helps remove LDL from your bloodstream, reducing the risk of cardiovascular problems. To improve heart health, it's beneficial to lower your LDL levels while maintaining or increasing your HDL levels.",
